MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_001: Urgh... I can't go on... It's too much...
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_002: Sofia! What's wrong? Are you sick?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_003: No, not sick. I'm...hungry. So hungry I feel faint...
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_004: Just hungry? That's a relief. I thought you were on\ndeath's door.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_005: Sorry to make you worry. I'm just so hungry...
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_006: If this is what you get like when you're hungry, I'd\nbetter get to work.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_007: And if you can't move, I'll carry you. I'm strong\nenough. Upsy-daisy!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_008: Thank you...Mikaela.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_009: Mmm! That was delicious! I feel like my old self\nagain. All thanks to you!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_010: I think I ate every last crumb. Once I get started,\nmy appetite takes over. Sorry for all the trouble.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_011: Nothing to apologize for. I'm sure you'll help me out\nwith something soon enough.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_012: Of course! Is there anything I can help you with right\nnow? Anything at all!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_013: Oh, no. As long as you're fine, then I'm fine too. Just\npromise you'll drop by next time you need a meal.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_014: Truth is, it's nice to cook for somebody who enjoys\nmy cooking like you do!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_015: That's really nice of you to say, but I owe you one.\nSeriously, thank you.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_016: I'll return your kindness one day. I swear.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_017: Hah! Oh, come on! It was just dinner.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_018: Just dinner?! There's no such thing. You're a true\nfriend, Miki.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_019: A true friend?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_020: Yes! I mean, food is life. And you shared some with\nme today. I don't take that lightly.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_C_021: Well, Sofia... You're awfully kind. I look forward to\nnext time.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_001: "Aged beans"? "Unique aroma"? I'd say they're\nunique! They smell like... Guh.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_002: Miki! What's got you all riled up?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_003: These coffee beans! That merchant sold me some\ncrap about how good they are, but they're...crap!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_004: Well, he doesn't know who he's fooling with. We'll\nsee if he changes his tune.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_005: I've got your back. It's the least I can do after you\nmade me that delicious meal.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_006: Hey, you! I can't brew these beans! If it's all the same\nto you, I'll have my refund.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_007: Easy, now! That's quite a claim. Let's calm down and\ntake it from the top.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_008: Hey, wait a second... I know you!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_009: Sofia? It is you! The boss's little girl!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_010: Sofia? You know this guy?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_011: Don't that beat all? You used to sit and play with my\ndice. Never once rolled snake eyes!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_012: Ha, I remember. But that was a while ago. It might\nbe time to leave all those games behind.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_013: Y-you're right. I gotta get on the straight and narrow\nonce and for all. You raised a good one, boss.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_014: Any friend of Sofia's is a friend of mine, y'hear? I\nnever shoulda sold you those beans. Here.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_015: Huh. OK. That was...a lot simpler than I thought it\nwould be.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_016: Well, you have your money. I'll see you ladies\nnext time.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_017: Take care of yourself! And no more bad beans!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_018: Who ARE you?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_019: Ehehe... My dad was a bandit chief. I've been\naround guys like that since I was little.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_020: He always wanted me to live a more respectable life,\nso he sent me away when I was 12.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_021: The guys always loved Dad though. Even now they\nstill see me as the chief's daughter. It can be helpful.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_022: But you probably don't want someone like me\nhanging around. At least I got to pay you back.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_023: Not so fast! Where do you think you're going?\nI haven't said my piece yet!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_024: Who cares whose daughter you are? You've got a\ngood heart. That's what counts.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_025: Miki...
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_026: If I don't care, neither should you. So come on back\nfor a home-cooked meal whenever you want!
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_027: Really? Who would say no to that? And don't worry.\nI'll keep finding ways to return the favor.
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_028: Are you kidding? You don't need to pay me back.\nWe're friends, right?
MID_SE_Mic_Sop_B_029: Hehe. We are. Thanks, Miki.